1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,437
Something in this lake smashed a fishing

2
00:00:02,447 --> 00:00:04,110
boat and threw two men overboard.

3
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:05,640
That's what the papers said.

4
00:00:05,870 --> 00:00:06,971
This is Bass Lake.

5
00:00:07,621 --> 00:00:10,996
In 1838, when it was called Cedar Lake, a

6
00:00:11,006 --> 00:00:13,010
Logansport paper printed a legend.

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,585
A monster was killed on its banks, it

8
00:00:15,595 --> 00:00:17,770
said; its bones could still be found.

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,839
Its mate escaped into the water.

10
00:00:20,489 --> 00:00:23,807
In 1893, papers said four men went fishing

11
00:00:23,817 --> 00:00:26,445
here, among them the sheriff and a lawyer

12
00:00:26,455 --> 00:00:28,062
who defended President Garfield's

13
00:00:28,072 --> 00:00:28,643
assassin.

14
00:00:29,093 --> 00:00:30,981
One hooked something that towed their boat

15
00:00:30,991 --> 00:00:31,803
for half an hour.

16
00:00:32,153 --> 00:00:34,007
Then it surfaced and smashed the stern

17
00:00:34,017 --> 00:00:34,673
with its tail.

18
00:00:34,903 --> 00:00:36,443
Forty feet long, they said,

19
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:38,537
greenish-black, with a huge pointed head.

20
00:00:39,087 --> 00:00:41,285
Bass Lake sits on a ridge with no stream

21
00:00:41,295 --> 00:00:42,017
flowing in.

22
00:00:42,247 --> 00:00:43,863
Springs and wells help fill it.

23
00:00:43,873 --> 00:00:45,916
Comment your town, and it could be next.

